{
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  // LOCAL BINDINGS ONLY — this is not a deployment config.
  //
  // Two jobs, both local:
  //
  //   1. Give `wrangler d1 ...` commands a binding, a database, and a
  //      migrations directory, so schema work can happen before any Worker
  //      exists. (The d1 section below; migration commands ignore the rest.)
  //   2. Give `getPlatformProxy()` the bindings `next dev` needs — D1 and,
  //      since Phase 9, a **locally simulated** R2 bucket.
  //
  // `r2_buckets` here does NOT mean a bucket exists in Cloudflare. Nothing in
  // this file creates a remote resource: miniflare simulates the bucket under
  // `.wrangler/state/v3`, with no account, no credentials and no network.
  // Creating the real bucket is still a human action — see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
  //
  // It is deliberately separate from the eventual OpenNext deployment configs
  // for `apps/web` and `apps/admin` because:
  //
  //   * Schema migrations are a repository-level concern owned by
  //     `migrations/`, not by either app. Both apps will eventually bind the
  //     same database; neither should own its migration history.
  //   * A deployment config needs compatibility dates, build output
  //     directories, routes, and per-environment bindings — none of which
  //     are decided yet (deployment is Phase 22). Guessing them now would
  //     bake in choices this phase has no basis to make.
  //   * Keeping them apart means running a migration can never accidentally
  //     publish a Worker.
  //
  // Contains no secrets. `database_id` is a resource identifier, not a
  // credential; authentication comes from the developer's own Wrangler
  // OAuth session and is never stored in the repository.
  //
  // Usage — run these from the REPOSITORY ROOT, where this file is. Wrangler
  // resolves `-c` relative to the working directory, so running them from an
  // app directory fails with a doubled path.
  //
  //   pnpm exec wrangler d1 migrations list  portfolio-cms --local -c wrangler.d1.jsonc
  //   pnpm exec wrangler d1 migrations apply portfolio-cms --local -c wrangler.d1.jsonc
  //
  // `--remote` applies to the live database and is an OWNER action, never the
  // agent's. It has to happen BEFORE deploying code that reads the new schema
  // — the other order returned 500 to every visitor once. See
  // docs/DEPLOYMENT.md and docs/DATABASE.md.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "portfolio-d1-admin",
  "d1_databases": [
    {
      "binding": "DB",
      "database_name": "portfolio-cms",
      "database_id": "1e85ce4f-d5e4-44e4-b589-e00992bc0b60",
      "migrations_dir": "migrations"
    }
  ],
  // Simulated locally by miniflare. No bucket of this name exists in
  // Cloudflare, and nothing here creates one.
  "r2_buckets": [
    {
      "binding": "MEDIA",
      "bucket_name": "portfolio-media"
    }
  ]
}
